## R7. FINDINGS LEDGER

### CRITICAL

**C1 — WZ-3(ii) is FALSE as stated, and the J-D0 routing it supports (§4b, §7)
is a mis-citation of J-D0's perimeter.**

The note, §3.6:

> "(ii) D_κ is a bijection of digit vectors fixing the top coefficient; it is a
> **type-preserving** bijection in J-D0's sense, being a slot-wise **unit
> character** (the multiplicative mode, not the additive one);"

and its proof:

> "*(ii) D_κ is invertible with inverse diag(ϑ_{μ−j}); it acts within each
> height's K-line, so it preserves which slots are occupied and each slot's
> type; multiplication by a fixed unit is a character, which is exactly the mode
> J-D0's blindness covers, and is exactly *not* the NONCHAR mode …*"

and §4(b):

> "**(b) The multiplicative half — INSIDE J-D0's perimeter, with the bijection
> exhibited.** The residual-convention change is the diagonal unit rescaling
> D_κ, i.e. a **slot-wise unit character** — the very mode `JD0-BOX-2` describes
> … and the opposite of the NONCHAR mode."

J-D0's type-preservation clause is not a slot-level statement; it is a
**residual-level** statement with an explicit functional form:

> "**(f) The induced action on residual polynomials preserves factorization type
> POINTWISE.** The slot character acts on the level-j residual polynomial by the
> variable rescaling σ_ξ : R(y) ↦ ξ^{−deg R}·R(ξ·y) (JA-RES's z^{−iA}·C_i slot
> form …). σ_ξ extends the identity of K_j to a degree-preserving K_j-algebra
> automorphism of K_j[y]; automorphisms carry factorizations to factorizations,
> so deg, monicity, irreducibility, ψ(0) ≠ 0, and the full factorization-degree
> multiset are preserved for EVERY R" (`JD0_PROOF_2026-08-08.md` L118–131)

σ_ξ acts on the coefficient of T^j by ξ^{j−deg R} — **geometric in j**. D_κ acts
by ϑ_{μ−j}^{−1} = η^{−⌊(μ−j)·i(κ)/e₁⌋}, whose exponent is a **floor function of
(μ−j), not linear in it**. D_κ is therefore not of J-D0's form, and it does not
preserve factorization type. That is not a subtlety — it is precisely the note's
own §5 headline:

> "2. **The conventions genuinely separate, and exactly when ϑ is live.**"

A bijection under which "(T−s)^μ" and "not a perfect power" trade places is by
definition not type-preserving. The note simultaneously asserts D_κ is
type-preserving (WZ-3 ii) and proves it is not (§5, WZ-A′). J-D0's own dichotomy
is also mis-applied: the NONCHAR tooth is *"an additive slot shift is a bijection
that breaks type preservation, hence counts"* (`JD0_PROOF` L224–225) — D_κ breaks
type preservation **without** breaking counts, so it is in neither of J-D0's two
boxes.

Independent evidence, from a leg I ran (see G1 for the instrument): in the
sealed GENHN row `V1E2 Zp q=3 N=4 h=1`, **972 of 972** live-wrap refine events
have their residual type *flipped* by D_κ (multiplicative read → `1sq`, i.e. the
α/perfect-square type; coherent read → `2`, i.e. INERT). Pointwise type
preservation fails at every single live-wrap event in the corpus's own sealed
data.

Knock-on to the note's proof of (iii):

> "*(iii) both sets are the D_κ-images of {(T−s′)^μ : s′ ∈ K^×}, of cardinality
> |K| − 1 …*"

They are not: the first set **is** that set in Γ-coordinates and the second is
its D_κ-**preimage**; they are different sets. And the closing generality —
"every count stratified by **slot heights** transports along D_κ" — does not
reach the counts GENHN-4 actually feeds, which are stratified by residual
**type** (#RAM / #2SIDED / #SPLTAIL / #SPLITEQ / #INERT / #ALPHA, `GENHN_PROOF`
L2525ff).

Knock-on to §7 and to the proposed ledger edit: §7 asserts *"this note consumes
J-D0 at FRAME grade with the bijection exhibited inline (§4b), so it neither
inherits nor enlarges BOX-2's perimeter"*, and the proposed replacement Display-A
line reads *"∧ JD0-BOX-2 -- FRAME-grade only; every consuming site exhibits its
own bijection"*. Both rest on C1.

**What survives.** The *conclusion* of §3.6 — that the count laws are
convention-blind — is TRUE, and I confirmed it empirically: in the same sealed
row the aggregate type census is identical at η = 1 and η = 2
(`'11'`: 486/486, `'1sq'`: 972/972, `'2'`: 1458/1458). But it is true for a
different reason than the note gives: D_κ is a bijection of the digit space
carrying the Γ-stratification onto the c-stratification, so corresponding strata
have equal cardinality — a pure relabelling argument that needs **no J-D0 at
all**. The honest repair is therefore strictly favourable to the note's ledger
claim (J-D0 not consumed here, rather than consumed inside its perimeter), but
it is a repair, not a reading, and it invalidates WZ-3(ii) as displayed.

The note also inherits this error from GENHN's frozen sentence *"counts are
twist-blind (J-D0: (digits) ↦ (twisted digits) is a type-preserving bijection),
LETTERS are twisted"* (L736–737) and from the audit's CLEAN-site list, which
calls the same bijection type-preserving at GENH4 L370–371. That mitigates
authorship but not correctness — and the note explicitly claims to be *"GENHN's
own sentence … made exact at μ ≥ 3"* (§3.6), when what §5 actually shows is that
half of GENHN's sentence is false at live ϑ.

